[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5458911705","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122952#issuecomment-5458911705","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122952","id":5458911705,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRWBh2Q","user":{"login":"Ansraer","id":6329420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjk0MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6329420?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer","html_url":"https://github.com/Ansraer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T23:44:05Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T23:44:05Z","body":"Please don't use AI to write pull requests. Furthermore, I don't think that the changes you committed make sense. From a quick glance it would appear that whatever AI model you used added a dependency to Carbon. The thing is that to my knowledge Carbon is a really old input framework, which Apple deprecated more than a decade ago.\r\n\r\nI would suggest you open an issue for the bug you encountered first and then personally look into modern solutions without using AI if you wish to work on this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5458911705/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5461516141","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122952#issuecomment-5461516141","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122952","id":5461516141,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRYgfbQ","user":{"login":"voidstarone","id":617663,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzY2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/617663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone","html_url":"https://github.com/voidstarone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-29T09:20:03Z","updated_at":"2026-08-29T09:20:03Z","body":"@Ansraer I did not use AI to write the pull request. I used AI to find the correct file and suggest a fix. I then tested this fix manually before getting the AI to write the automated tests; it is my understanding that this is within the contribution guidelines. The pull request itself is written by hand.\r\n\r\nI did _not_ add any dependency whatsoever. The Carbon import exists in the original file as you can see here:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/platform/macos/key_mapping_macos.mm","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5461516141/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5463409758","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122952#issuecomment-5463409758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122952","id":5463409758,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRaUEXg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-29T16:00:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-29T16:00:25Z","body":"Would it be possible to file an issue for the broken behavior as well? It's unclear what precisely the previous, undesirable behavior was, and thus how this PR's behavior \"fixes\" it.\r\n\r\nFor others who may also not be familiar with Dvorak-Qwerty: [this page](https://github.com/kentonv/dvorak-qwerty) describes it in more detail. According to them, holding ⌘ causes the keyboard to temporarily switch to a Qwerty layout, so that keyboard shortcuts use the existing standard Qwerty key positions. So, a user with a keyboard whose keys have the Dvorak layout printed on them would use (according to the letters printed on their keys) ⌘J for copy, ⌘Q for cut, and ⌘K for paste since J, Q, and K in the Dvorak layout are where the C, X, and V keys are in the Qwerty layout respectively, for example.\r\n\r\nI am on macOS and as such may be able to test this PR (or another implementation of it, if you choose to make one) in a couple of days, but I haven't had the opportunity to test this one. In the meantime, I am curious how this translates to the display of shortcuts in the UI. For Dvorak-Qwerty users, do menus display the shortcut for copy as ⌘C or as ⌘J? It seems to me like it should be the latter, since a user looking down at their keyboard would have to press the key labeled J (assuming a keyboard with Dvorak letters printed). But I don't know what the convention is for Dvorak and Dvorak-Qwerty users – maybe they're used to understanding displayed keyboard shortcuts being in the Qwerty layout?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5463409758/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5467824420","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122952#issuecomment-5467824420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122952","id":5467824420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRehhJA","user":{"login":"voidstarone","id":617663,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzY2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/617663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone","html_url":"https://github.com/voidstarone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidstarone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-30T09:13:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-30T09:13:25Z","body":"@Meorge for DQ users, the shortcuts display as usual cmd-C is Copy and displays that way, even though the key marked C produced J in Dvorak. This is the correct fix for the behaviour that all Apple's apps have.\r\n\r\nThe worst offender is Cut. Because the key marked X is Q in Dvorak. This means if one cuts without thinking too hard, they will quit the app. Annoying! \r\n\r\nHow can I file the issue for the broken behaviour?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5467824420/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5469258469","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122952#issuecomment-5469258469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122952","id":5469258469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRf5C5Q","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url