/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-30T15:47:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-30T15:47:15Z","body":"I'm on macOS 26.6.2 and Godot 4.8 master, and am also finding I can't reproduce the described issue (assuming I am understanding it correctly).\r\n\r\nI have a physical QWERTY keyboard. If I press the keys labeled ⌘S (i.e., ⌘ along with the key two keys to the right of the Caps Lock key) on my QWERTY keyboard:\r\n- When set to the \"Dvorak\" layout (_not_ \"Dvorak – QWERTY ⌘\"), I get the \"Open Scene\" window (expected, as the S key on a QWERTY keyboard is the O key on a Dvorak layout).\r\n- When set to the \"Dvorak – QWERTY ⌘\" layout, I get the \"Save Scene As...\" window (expected, since I was holding ⌘ so it temporarily shifted back to use the QWERTY layout).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5469670833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5476144176","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122952#issuecomment-5476144176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122952","id":5476144176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRmdUMA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url"